{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"unfleshly-peerless-grayfox","creation_channel":"cli","description":"## Observed\n\n`make verify` on 2026-09-06 failed with **33 failures, 29 of them identical**:\n\n    rebar.llm.errors.GateCongestedError: gate admission refused: all 4 concurrent gate\n    slot(s) on this host are in use\n\nAffected files: `tests/unit/test_plan_review_retry.py` (17), `test_plan_review_reuse.py` (5),\n`test_opcert_producer_seam_8d8e.py` (2), `workflow/test_gate_error_sidecar_heldout.py` (2),\n`test_plan_review_cli_retry.py` (1, surfacing as `assert 11 == 2` — exit 11 is the transient\nretry code), `test_plan_relation_snapshot.py` (1),\n`test_completion_wrapper_duration_instrumentation.py` (1),\n`interfaces/lifecycle/test_plan_review_sign_transaction_lifecycle.py` (1).\n\n## Root cause, established by measurement rather than inferred\n\nIt is NOT xdist contention. It reproduces **single-threaded, with `-p no:randomly -x`**.\n\nThe slot directory is host-wide:\n\n    /var/folders/.../T/rebar-gate-snapshots/locks/gate-slot-{0,1,2,3}\n\n`lsof` on those files during the failure named the holders, and none of them belonged to this\nworktree:\n\n    python3.1  7168  .../comment-gates-current/.venv/bin/rebar review-plan sphalerite-bereft-tortoise\n    python3.1 14552  .../fix-caused-by-lagging-checkout/.venv/bin/pytest -n 4 ...\n    (plus 48444, 85788, 90624)\n\nSo **another agent's `rebar review-plan`, and another agent's test run, in different\nworktrees, were holding the slots this suite needs.** That is the admission bound working as\ndesigned — it is a per-HOST bound (ADR 0112 decision 5), and `_slot_dir()` deliberately\nfollows `REBAR_GATE_TMPDIR` so the counter covers every process on the box.\n\nThe defect is that these TESTS opt into that shared bound. `tests/unit/test_gate_admission_09da.py`\ndoes not have the problem: its `gate_host` fixture sets `REBAR_GATE_TMPDIR` to a `tmp_path`,\nso it gets its own slot directory. The files above do not, so they inherit the real one.\n\n## Why this matters beyond one red run\n\n1. It makes `make verify` non-deterministic on any machine running more than one rebar\n   process — which is this project's normal operating mode (\"rebar is driven by MANY local\n   agent processes at once\"; bug `icicled-unstable-urial`).\n2. It is indistinguishable, from the log alone, from a real regression. The failure is a\n   `GateCongestedError` raised from production code, not a fixture error, so an author who\n   has just touched anything gate-adjacent will reasonably suspect their own change. That\n   cost was paid on story `cryptozoic-unlit-ladybug`.\n3. `recheck`/re-run is the wrong response and AGENTS.md forbids it as a habit. The fix is\n   isolation, not retry.\n\n## Suggested fix\n\nGive the affected modules the same `REBAR_GATE_TMPDIR` isolation `test_gate_admission_09da.py`\nalready uses. The narrow version is a fixture in each affected module; the better version is\none shared fixture, since the property wanted is \"no unit test contends for the host's real\ngate slots\" rather than \"these eight files do not\".\n\nWhether that fixture should be autouse across the unit suite needs care: `autouse_fixture` is\na censused kind under the shrink-only mechanism ratchet, so it needs a `mechanism-ok` marker\nand a reason.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] AC1 The affected modules pass while another process on the same host holds all four\n      real gate slots. Reproduce by taking the slots (e.g. a held `flock` on each\n      `gate-slot-N`) and running the suite.\n- [ ] AC2 No unit test acquires a slot in the host's real `rebar-gate-snapshots/locks`\n      directory. A guard asserting this is preferable to fixing the eight files by hand.\n- [ ] AC3 `tests/unit/test_gate_admission_09da.py`'s own isolation is unchanged.\n\n## NOT established\n\n- Whether every one of the 29 failures has this single cause. They share the exception and\n  the message, and the holders were foreign processes, but each was not individually traced.\n- Whether the same contention affects the `integration`/`external` lanes.","id":"863f-52ef-c3a8-4794","parent_id":"","priority":2,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"bug","title":"Gate-exercising unit tests contend on the HOST-WIDE gate slot directory, so any concurrent rebar process on the same machine fails them"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1788668828925099001,"uuid":"dd22297f-68f0-4a6f-a281-9d838364d8c1"}